hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27578","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl, from his father, that he heard Umm al-Darda say: I came out of the bathhouse and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met me and said: From where, O Umm al-Darda? She said: From the bathhouse. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, no woman removes her clothes in other than the house of one of her mothers except she tears every veil between her and the Most Merciful."
"27579","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Rushdayn narrated to us, he said: Zabban narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, that he heard Umm al-Darda say: I came out of the bathhouse and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met me, and he mentioned it."
"27580","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah al-Duali, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, raising the hadith, she said: Whoever garrisons in any of the Muslim coasts three days, it suffices him for a year's garrison."
"27581","Harun narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: And Haywah said: Abu Sakhr informed me that Yuhannas Abu Musa narrated to him that Umm al-Darda narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met her one day and said: From where have you come, O Umm al-Darda? She said: From the bathhouse. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: No woman removes her clothes except she tears what is between her and Allah, Exalted and Glorious, of veil."
